"sponsorshipDate":"2026-06-24","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NC"},{"bioguideId":"M001230","fullName":"Rep. Mackenzie, Ryan [R-PA-7]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-08-31","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"PA"},{"bioguideId":"G000599","fullName":"Rep. Goldman, Daniel S. [D-NY-10]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-09-14","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NY"},{"bioguideId":"D000399","fullName":"Rep. Doggett, Lloyd [D-TX-37]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-09-14","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"TX"},{"bioguideId":"P000613","fullName":"Rep. Panetta, Jimmy [D-CA-19]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-09-14","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CA"},{"bioguideId":"V000129","fullName":"Rep. Valadao, David G. [R-CA-22]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-09-15","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CA"},{"bioguideId":"D000530","fullName":"Rep. Deluzio, Christopher R. [D-PA-17]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-09-15","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"PA"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T18:58:28+00:00","id":"hr349-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-13","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-02-14","text":"Referred to the Subcommittee on Livestock, Dairy, and Poultry."},"laws":[],"number":"349","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Animals","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"M000317","district":11,"fullName":"Rep. Malliotakis, Nicole [R-NY-11]","party":"R","state":"NY"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-01-13","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>Goldie's Act</strong></p><p>This bill expands enforcement provisions under the Animal Welfare Act (AWA).</p><p>Specifically, the bill directs the Department of Agriculture (USDA) to document and record detailed descriptions of violations of the act observed during inspections and investigations. USDA must provide a copy of all records documenting violations to state, local, and municipal animal control or law enforcement officials within 24 hours of such inspections or investigations.</p><p>Inspections must be held at least once a year of each research facility, the premises of each animal dealer, and each exhibitor of animals. If violations are found during inspections, then USDA must conduct any necessary follow-up inspections until all the violations are corrected. Inspectors must confiscate or destroy in a humane manner animals found to be suffering physical or psychological harm as a result of failure to comply with the AWA.</p><p>Violators are subject to civil penalties as outlined in the bill.</p>","updateDate":"2025-03-31T14:57:09Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Goldie’s Act","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-09-16T08:09:15Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-09-16T08:09:15Z"}
